<title>PERU: Peru's net int'l reserves rise to $9.099 billion.</title>
<headline>Peru's net int'l reserves rise to $9.099 billion.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's Central Reserve Bank said on Monday its net international reserves rose to $9.099 billion at the end of February from $9.087 billion the previous week.</p>
<p>As at the end of 1996 reserves were $8.540 billion.</p>
<p>The government estimates Peru's international reserves will rise above $10 billion by mid-1998.</p>
<p>-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
